    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n### The Problem\nThe `gate` subcommand in the `frai` CLI was not properly passing the `--ci` flag to `frai-gate`. This happened because Commander's argument parsing was interfering with the pass-through of arguments.\n\n### The Solution\nI modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to use `process.argv` directly instead of relying on Commander's argument parsing for the `gate` subcommand. The fix:\n\n1. Removed `[args...]` from `.command('gate')`\n2. Changed the action to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` after the `'gate'` subcommand\n3. Pass those arguments unmodified to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n\n### Changes Made\n- **packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts**: Updated the gate command implementation\n- **packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js**: Rebuilt the compiled output\n\n### Verification\nThe fix has been tested and confirmed working:\n```bash\nnode packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci\n```\n\u2713 Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`  \n\u2713 Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the workflow file that was missing before)\n\nThe changes are minimal and focused, affecting only the `gate` command delegation in the CLI.",
